{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_93","type":"agent_message","text":"The steering stress test is a null against its controls: both + and − authorship steering changed the aggregate binary outcome by +6.25 points, exactly matched by one random direction; the other random directions ranged 0 to +6.25. Because opposite signs moved the same way and the effect was not outside random controls, it fails the preregistered causal criterion. I’m adding the probe-logit shift calculation and then moving to final validation/reporting."}}
