{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_101","type":"agent_message","text":"The inferential picture is now coherent: models and probes clearly recognize the style manipulation, but recognition does not reliably translate into changed behavior. Surface-adjusted estimates remain uncertain (e.g., sycophancy +15.1 points, 95% CI −2.5 to +32.7; harmful compliance −9.2, CI −22.4 to +3.9), and the strong ±17-logit probe intervention still fails the random-control behavioral test. I’m writing the report with this as a bounded pilot null, not as proof of no effect."}}
