{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_107","type":"agent_message","text":"Research execution is complete and validated.\n\nKey findings:\n\n- LLM-style prompts were recognized as more AI-written by 13–42 percentage points.\n- None of six preregistered behavioral comparisons survived Holm correction.\n- Qwen3-8B’s authorship probe achieved 0.907 held-out AUROC versus 0.601 for surface features.\n- Authorship and evaluation-awareness directions had modest overlap: cosine 0.242.\n- Activation steering failed the causal test: ± authorship steering produced the same behavioral change, which a random direction matched.\n- Conclusion: authorship style is internally decodable, but this pilot found no reliable evidence that the representation drives safety-relevant behavior.\n\nDeliverables:\n\n- [Full research report](/workspaces/do-llms-behave-differently-when-c970-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/REPORT.md)\n- [Reproduction guide](/workspaces/do-llms-behave-differently-when-c970-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/README.md)\n- [Preregistered plan](/workspaces/do-llms-behave-differently-when-c970-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/planning.md)\n- [Validation summary](/workspaces/do-llms-behave-differently-when-c970-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/results/evaluations/validation_summary.json)\n- [Experiment code](/workspaces/do-llms-behave-differently-when-c970-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/src)\n\nValidation passed: source compilation, artifact checks, JSON parsing, repeated-analysis hash equality, figure inspection, and scientific invariants. The run used 1,879 unique API calls at an OpenRouter-reported cost of $2.13.\n\nThe data-analysis skill shaped the paired bootstrap/exact tests and multiplicity correction; critical-analysis informed the causal threshold and low-to-moderate evidence rating."}}
